WEBVTT

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.770
What? Then Sayu-chan's going home?

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.100
Yeah.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.360
I see.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.390
I guess they say it can all end 
in an instant, but...

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.440
It's still really sudden, right?

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:19.500
But if this gets her back to a normal life, 
it may be better for the both of you.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.780
I guess not, from the look on your face.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:32.000
Given that she ran away from home, 
I could kind of tell...

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.100
But her parents are kind of...

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:35.980
I see.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.370
But her brother is on her side, right?

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.180
Well, probably.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.200
Then you have to leave it to him.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.600
It's not your place as an outsider 
to get involved in their family problems.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.640
Yeah, I guess.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:38.130
"Proof"

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:54.400
I'm terribly sorry for the rude things 
I said the other day.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.570
No, it's fine.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.400
Please don't bow.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.020
No, but...

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.970
I think Sayu was really lucky 
to meet a man like you.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:13.630
No, you're exaggerating.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:18.380
Why did you do all this for her?

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.200
Why?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.200
Yes.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:29.040
The day I met Sayu, I was really drunk.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.220
A girl I'd liked had just rejected me.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:36.570
And on the way home, 
I found her crouching on the street.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:38.420
Oh, so that's it.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.070
I'd always wondered myself.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.180
But I finally understand.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:50.260
I think it's because she was cute.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.380
I'm sorry. That's kind of a bad answer.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.020
I think it's a fine answer.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:02.870
It's so honest that it's hard 
to believe. I like it.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:11.550
Did she tell you anything about her mother?

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.100
Not really...

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.230
I see.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.160
Do you know of a company 
called Ogiwara Foods?

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.170
Yes.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:23.490
Our father was its president.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:28.350
But he had a thing for affairs.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.840
By the time our mother 
was pregnant with Sayu,

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.080
he'd already moved on to another woman.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.540
He asked her to get an abortion.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.590
Of course, she refused.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.800
She gave birth to Sayu, hoping it would give
her one last chance to keep her husband.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.260
But our father left us,

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:56.980
and to our mother, Sayu simply became proof 
that her husband didn't love her anymore.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:01.050
I think you've heard from Sayu 
what happened next.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.680
When she was little, she was a happy kid.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.450
Full of energy. Completely normal.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.290
But her mother didn't love her 
in the slightest.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.540
When she was old enough to realize that,

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.890
the smile almost entirely
disappeared from her face.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:24.470
I believe a parent's love
is critical for a child.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.790
In that sense,

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:34.060
you may be the first
parent-like person in her life.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:41.480
Thank you for caring about Sayu.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:42.810
No, I...

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.320
I didn't do anything.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:50.140
There are only a few days left, 
but please continue to be by her side.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:52.530
Yes, I will.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.750
What did my brother say?

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:01.840
He said he wanted to apologize.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.340
I see.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:07.400
He really does care about you.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.300
Yeah, he does.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:18.030
I've caused problems for both you and him.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.900
I know that, but...

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.270
I'm still scared to go home.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.950
But I know I have to. 
So I'm going to make sure I'm ready.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:38.250
But until then, 
I can enjoy my life here, right?

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:40.580
Yeah.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:44.340
We ran so late today.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.110
I'm going to miss my movie.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:47.770
Here.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:48.700
Thanks.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:53.370
Sorry for keeping you so late.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:56.520
It's fine. It involves our project, too.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.680
I can always count on you to help us out.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:01.990
I'll take your place 
on another business trip soon.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.940
Here, take this.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:05.940
<b>Easy Book of Recipes</b>

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.540
What's this?

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:11.200
I don't want you going back to eating stuff 
from the convenience store.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.010
<b>(Serves 2)</b>

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.300
<b>Ingredients</b>

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.050
<b>No Need to Fry!</b>

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.620
<b>Sweet and Sour Pork</b>

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.040
Use this to cook once in a while.

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:17.740
Wow...

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.960
I put the ones you liked first.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.580
So I hope you'll use it.

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:25.050
Sure. Thanks.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.410
You're welcome.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.930
Want to go eat out?

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:35.770
That sounds nice. 
Let's go somewhere kind of fancy.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:38.350
Yoshida, you want to get lunch?

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.810
Oh, um...

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.520
Sorry, I'm not at a stopping point. 
I'll pass.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.690
Okay...

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.530
You should get some rest.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.870
I'm taking my smoke breaks.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.050
That's not what I meant.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:11.400
Thank you for the meal.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:12.550
Hey, Yoshida-san...

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.260
There's someplace I want to go.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:17.720
This late?

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.150
Yeah.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.240
It has to be this late.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.970
I never knew this place existed.

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:28.010
Right?

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:32.170
When Asami took me here the first time, 
I couldn't believe it.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:37.120
When I came here, Asami told me...

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:37.990
Told you what?

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.830
Compared to the stars, we're all so tiny.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:47.960
But we all have our own pasts, 
and futures, too.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:53.900
When I heard that, 
I felt kind of safe... and I cried.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.680
Safe?

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:01.680
Yeah. Asami heard about my
awful past and didn't reject me.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:03.720
She told me that I really hung in there.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.300
I see.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:06.850
But...

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:12.630
Part of it was forgiveness, 
but part of it was reality.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.030
No matter how many years I live after this,

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:23.770
the fact that I ran all the way here 
will stay a part of my past.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.160
Yeah.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:31.500
No matter what anyone says, 
that'll never disappear.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:38.570
But Yoshida-san...

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:46.090
At the end of my awful life 
as a runaway, I met you.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:52.760
If I hadn't met you, 
I would've kept avoiding facing my mistake.

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.740
I might've ended up somewhere worse.

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:01.510
Everything got better when I met you.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:05.330
I'm so happy that I almost want 
to stay here forever.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:09.080
When I'm with you, I'm so happy.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.140
It gets harder and harder to leave.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:20.540
So this week, I tried a bunch of times 
to leave while you weren't there.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:23.340
But I couldn't.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:28.840
Really... I want to stay here forever.

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:38.150
But you know... I can't.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:43.120
If I stay here forever, I'll never face my past. 
I'll never put an end to it.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:47.200
I'll just keep running from it.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:53.290
Ogiwara Sayu's past will be one 
of just running away.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:54.250
And then...

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.190
Sayu...

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:05.740
So I want to prove it...

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:07.790
"Prove it"?

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:08.680
Yeah.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:15.230
Prove that my meeting you 
was a good thing in my life.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:20.620
I want to prove it not just to myself, 
but in a way that anybody can see.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:28.620
And when that happens, I think 
I might just be able to live on my own.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:30.580
I see...

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:36.970
Because I met you, Yoshida-san...

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:44.730
Just because I met you... 
That's the only reason.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:47.940
That's what I'm taking back home.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.410
So...

00:11:56.470 --> 00:11:57.740
Be there to cheer me on.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.320
Yeah...

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.180
Of course I will.

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:19.460
Is it tomorrow when Sayu-chan's going home?

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:21.140
Yeah.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.100
She'll be missed.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.680
You never met her.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.260
No, you'll miss her.

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:37.980
At least go home on time today 
and enjoy your last moments with her.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:42.710
Why not just follow her to Hokkaido?

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.480
Is it that surprising an idea?

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:48.160
I assumed you were thinking of it.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.920
I'm not part of her family.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:52.370
It would be weird.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:56.360
Everything you've done 
this whole time is weird.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:59.290
What about work?

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:03.740
This company won't go under 
just because one person leaves.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:05.520
Right, Hashimoto-senpai?

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:08.080
Huh? Yeah...

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:11.210
Thankfully, everything's going well right now.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.630
You heard him.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:20.710
Sayu is trying to face this on her own.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:24.110
It wouldn't help her 
if I tried to get too involved.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:29.870
Does it matter right now 
if it helps her or not?

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:35.040
Is it really something 
she has to face alone?

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.500
Well...

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:47.430
<b>Yuuki Asami</b>

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.490
What does she want?

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:55.640
Hello?

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:58.280
<i>Do you know where Sayu-chan went?</i>

00:13:58.280 --> 00:13:59.230
What's wrong?

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.730
She's not picking up her phone.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.000
<i>I can't find her anywhere.</i>

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.650
<i>I'll go look for her a little more.</i>

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.230
<i>If you find out anything, call me.</i>

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:07.900
R-Right...

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:16.460
<i>The number you have called 
is out of range or turned off.</i>

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:17.560
No way...

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.720
What's wrong?

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:20.830
Sayu disappeared.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.580
You need to go find her!

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:30.040
I'm not feeling well, 
so I'm going home early.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:34.260
Yoshida's not feeling well, either. 
I'll make sure he gets home okay.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:37.100
Understood.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.730
Thanks.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.850
Let's get going. 
Get your things together.

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:44.480
But this is still due...

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.200
Anybody here who can handle 
Yoshida's work today?

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:48.950
Me.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:51.350
I'll take it.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.870
Thanks, Mishima-san!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.060
Now there's no problem, right, Yoshida?

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:59.450
Y-Yeah...

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:09.560
To be honest, when you said
you took in a teenage girl,

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:14.030
I kind of figured this would happen.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:16.100
Figured what would happen?

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:20.310
That you wouldn't be able 
to think about anything else.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.630
That's not happening.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:22.830
It sure as hell is.

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:26.390
She's the only thing on your mind lately.

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:35.900
It pisses me off, seeing it.

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:37.450
What does?

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:42.030
You know exactly what it is you care about.

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:43.920
But you're pretending you don't.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:49.380
And it really pisses me off.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.480
What was that shit about your deadlines?

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:56.100
You looked like you wanted 
to run out of the room.

00:15:57.570 --> 00:16:00.930
If you don't figure what it is 
you care about, it'll be too late.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:05.300
You're scared to death 
of her going home alone, right?

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:07.230
I...

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:09.530
You might admit that.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:13.620
But what you won't admit is that
you're scared of being apart from her.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.690
No, I just want her to be happy.

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:22.830
Do you think she'll be happy, then, 
if she goes back home alone?

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.510
I can see it on your face.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.950
I can tell.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:32.100
You're my best friend.

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:38.230
You two can't be separated anymore.

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:41.290
If you're worried, go with her, 
or do whatever you want.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.100
Not you, too...

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.390
Your work will be fine.

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:47.560
And right now, who even cares?

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:51.220
No, that's being too irresponsible.

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.710
The whole project depends on me.

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:58.870
Doesn't Sayu-chan depend on you, too?

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:04.810
Isn't it much more irresponsible to tell her 
to do her best on her own,

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:06.780
when she wants your help?

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:08.330
Well...

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:11.260
It's the same. The exact same.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:15.470
All that matters now is 
which is more important to you.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.260
I won't say anything else.

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:23.370
Just make your decision.

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:27.800
Gotou-san?

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:29.930
Yes, this is Yoshida.

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:40.440
What were you thinking?!

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:43.610
I'm sorry.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:46.670
She wanted to see where you worked.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.200
She said she was waiting 
to walk home with you.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.460
Cute, huh?

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:56.840
You should've just said so.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.640
It wouldn't be a surprise, then.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.220
Don't you get it, Yoshida-cchi?

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:06.830
At least make sure 
I can get a hold of you.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:10.860
Sorry, I guess my phone ran out of battery.

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.520
Seriously...

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:18.030
I wish you could've seen how pale he was 
when he ran out of the room.

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:21.000
Don't tell her that!

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:22.920
Sorry.

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:26.700
You really lose it whenever
Sayu-chaso's involved, don't you?

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:28.800
This is all your fault to begin with.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:31.840
Um, I'm really sorry about today.

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:35.190
And causing problems for you all 
on the very last day I'm here.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:40.300
Don't be silly.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.740
You and I are best buds!

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:45.770
I hope you do well back in Hokkaido.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:47.470
Thank you.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:50.020
I'll be there to see you off tomorrow.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.520
Huh? You don't have to...

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:55.280
Listen, do you not know 
what "best buds" means?

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:56.230
She's a lot cuter than you made her sound.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.660
S-Sorry...

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:09.830
Hey, Yoshida-san.

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:13.040
Oh, you're up?

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:16.420
It'll be a long day tomorrow. 
Get some rest.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.180
Sayu?

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:22.810
Yoshida-san, can I get on the bed?

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:27.930
Sure, I guess... but why?

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.220
It's my last day here.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:33.400
You're not going to do anything, right?

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:35.610
I guess.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:47.200
Move over a little.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.790
Okay.

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:59.220
We've lived together for so long, 
but this is the first time we've been so close.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.820
Yeah.

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:04.660
Don't worry. I won't do anything weird.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.010
If I do, you'll kick me out.

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:12.170
Yeah. I won't even wait till tomorrow.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:13.990
That would be a problem.

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:19.960
Hey...

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:22.330
Let me do this just for a little.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:30.660
Yoshida-san...

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:37.250
If you were my dad, 
would I have grown up into a normal girl?

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:44.650
I'm not your dad.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:47.840
Yeah, I know.

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:51.050
I'm just a guy who let you
stay in his apartment.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:52.220
Yeah.

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:56.240
It was kind and warm.

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:58.030
The best place to stay I could ask for.

00:20:58.030 --> 00:21:00.100
I'm glad to hear it.

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:05.850
So... leaving a place that's so warm...

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:23.420
The best place you've ever stayed 
has one last surprise for you.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.760
I'll go to Hokkaido with you.

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:35.650
You're scared to go alone, right?

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:37.660
I'll go keep an eye on you.

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:39.960
Really?

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.820
Yeah, really.

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:45.930
I'll go see your mom with you.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.320
Ow!

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:53.190
Yoshida-san... Thank you!

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:59.500
Yeah, you're welcome.

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:35.010
"Resolve"

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>See You Next Week</b>
